      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To simplify \\((1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)(1 + \\tan 25^\\circ)\\), we can use the tangent addition formula. The formula states that \\(\\tan (a + b) = \\frac{\\tan a + \\tan b}{1 - \\tan a \\tan b}\\). \n\nWe set \\(a = 20^\\circ\\) and \\(b = 25^\\circ\\), so \\(a + b = 45^\\circ\\). Using the tangent addition formula, we get:\n\\[\n\\tan 45^\\circ = \\tan (20^\\circ + 25^\\circ) = \\frac{\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ}{1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ}\n\\]\nSince \\(\\tan 45^\\circ = 1\\), we have:\n\\[\n1 = \\frac{\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ}{1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ}\n\\]\nMultiplying both sides by \\(1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ\\) gives:\n\\[\n1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ = \\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ\n\\]\nRearranging terms, we get:\n\\[\n1 = \\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ + \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ\n\\]\nNow, we return to the original problem, \\((1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)(1 + \\tan 25^\\circ)\\). Using the sum of angles formula for tangent:\n\\[\n\\tan (x + y) = \\frac{\\tan x + \\tan y}{1 - \\tan x \\tan y}, \\quad \\tan (x + y) = \\frac{\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ}{1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ}\n\\]\nWe analyze the left side of the equation:\n\\[\n(1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)(1 + \\tan 25^\\circ) = 1 + \\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ + \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ\n\\]\nSince \\(\\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ = 1 - 1 = 0\\), the right side of the original equation becomes 1:\n\\[\n1 + \\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ + 0 = 1 + (\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ) = 1\n\\]\nTherefore, the expression is simplified to:\n\\[\n\\boxed{2}\n\\]",
